    "17786893180b60ea14": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_editorial_callout_section_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-callout-section",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1100,
            "left_column_width": 45,
            "right_column_width": 55,
            "column_gap": 50,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "What this means when you are shopping",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "mobile_heading_size": 28,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_indent": 0,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 0,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/magnific_luxury-perfume-comparison_74h5S6MJAL.jpg_1.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 500,
            "heading_image_gap": 16,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 20,
            "body_text": "<p>When evaluating an inspired fragrance against an original, resist the urge to smell your wrist the exact second you spray. All fine fragrances need 2 to 3 minutes for the alcohol carrier to disperse.</p><p>Judge the fragrance at the 15-minute mark, the 2-hour mark, and the end of the day. Notice the trail of scent (the sillage) you leave when walking through a room. That is where high-quality formulation truly shines.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 17,
            "mobile_body_size": 15,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
